<title>SWEDEN: Committee rules to tax Skanska's Sandvik deal.</title>
<headline>Committee rules to tax Skanska's Sandvik deal.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish construction group Skanska said on Thursday a tax committee ruled it should pay capital gains tax on its sale of shares in tool and engineering group Sandvik.</p>
<p>Skanska has said the deal was worth roughly 10 billion crowns and would generate a capital gain of around 9.1 billion crowns.</p>
<p>Skanska will take the case to Sweden's Supreme Administrative Court, the highest court for tax issues of this kind, and expects a decision after the year-end, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The tax committee was split on the issue with four members and the chairman being in favour of Skanska paying capital gains tax and four members being against, Skanska said.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
